for the\n\u003e sample ATT SIM? Thank you.\n\u003e\n\u003e Oscar\n\u003e\n\u003e *From: *Andy Cutright \u003candy.cutright@optconnect.com\u003e\n\u003e *Date: *Thursday, July 30, 2026 at 11:38 AM\n\u003e *To: *Jonathan Gilbert \u003cjonathangilbert@novacharge.net\u003e\n\u003e *Cc: *mark.parreno@optconnect.com \u003cmark.parreno@optconnect.com\u003e; Oscar\n\u003e Rodriguez \u003coscarrodriguez@novacharge.net\u003e; Marilyn Rodriguez \u003c\n\u003e marilynrodriguez@novacharge.net\u003e; rob.smith@optconnect.com \u003c\n\u003e rob.smith@optconnect.com\u003e; lacey.hataway@optconnect.com \u003c\n\u003e lacey.hataway@optconnect.com\u003e; net-eng@optconnect.com \u003c\n\u003e net-eng@optconnect.com\u003e\n\u003e *Subject: *Re: OptConnect - NovaCharge - Follow up meeting\n\u003e\n\u003e Hi Jonathan,\n\u003e\n\u003e Following up from our call. We've completed the analysis on the physical\n\u003e AT&T unit; to finish the eSIM side and tie the finding to the usage, we\n\u003e still need one trace from an affected eSIM device — the same set you pulled\n\u003e before:\n\u003e\n\u003e - traceroute, nslookup, and interface / network-manager state\n\u003e\n\u003e Once we have that, we'll confirm the root cause and move to the billing\n\u003e and remediation discussion.\n\u003e\n\u003e Thanks,\n\u003e Andy\n\u003e\n\u003e On Wed, Jul 08, 2026 03:43 PM, mark.parreno@optconnect.com wrote:\n\u003e\n\u003e Mark Parreno is inviting you to a scheduled Zoom meeting.\n\u003e\n\u003e Topic: OptConnect - NovaCharge - Follow up meeting\n\u003e Time: Jul 16, 2026 01:00 PM Pacific Time (US and Canada)\n\u003e Join Zoom Meeting\n\u003e\n\u003e https://optconnect.zoom.us/j/86710354080?pwd\u001cXWHjdwEaSm2nZGKbvnq1z6CxBQ7f.1\n\u003e\n\u003e Meeting chat link\n\u003e https://optconnect.zoom.us/launch/jc/86710354080\n\u003e\n\u003e Meeting ID: 867 1035 4080\n\u003e Passcode: t4_nYXCj{`\n\u003e\n\u003e ---\n\u003e\n\u003e One tap mobile\n\u003e +13863475053,,86710354080# US\n\u003e +15074734847,,8